/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T17:46:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T17:46:15Z","body":"This appears to happen with the `memoryBarrierShared` and `barrier` functions. On D3D12 with Intel, they seem to be ignored for some reason. If I put a `memoryBarrier` before these, the issue is fixed.\n\nBut there's another catch. The Mesa SPIR-V to DXIL converter appears to emit barriers with the `UAVFenceThreadGroup` flag, which DirectXShaderCompiler never does. The `memoryBarrier` call in particular did not have this flag but the other ones did. \n\nSo maybe the driver is not recognizing the flag and skips the barrier instruction. Or the barriers are just not working properly in the first place. I'll be testing these scenarios.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4390580587/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4391175741","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116053#issuecomment-4391175741","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116053","id":4391175741,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBbwGPQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https:/